invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_ifma_product.h
catches: rsa_ifma_model_test
reason: digits_to_words never takes a third digit into a word, so a word
  that starts more than 40 bits into a digit loses its top bits, which
  the digit two above holds. RSA-2048's fifth word is one. Each
  public operation's result is then wrong, and bin/rsa_ifma_model_test
  compares rsa_vp1_cpu under the bit with rsa_vp1.

--- old
            word |= value_at_or_zero(digits, digit_count, j + 2) << (104 - offset);
--- new
            word |= 0;
